WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.031
Agent monitoring should cover operational
quality as well as security.

2
00:00:07.111 --> 00:00:13.963
Model errors, unsupported claims at a high
level, low-confidence outputs,

3
00:00:14.043 --> 00:00:21.002
tool timeouts, retry behavior, response
latency, rate limits, cost spikes,

4
00:00:21.082 --> 00:00:28.577
degraded provider performance, and failed
retrieval can all affect user trust and

5
00:00:28.657 --> 00:00:30.477
business outcomes.

6
00:00:30.557 --> 00:00:38.051
A secure agent that frequently times out
or returns unsupported answers will not be

7
00:00:38.131 --> 00:00:41.450
reliable enough for production use.

8
00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:48.383
Prompt and model changes need monitoring
because they can change behavior.

9
00:00:48.463 --> 00:00:54.779
A new prompt version may improve
helpfulness but increase tool calls.

10
00:00:54.859 --> 00:01:00.320
A model update may reduce latency but
change response style.

11
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:07.466
A retrieval configuration change may
reduce cost but miss important sources.

12
00:01:07.546 --> 00:01:13.542
Regression testing signals, evaluation
results, user feedback,

13
00:01:13.622 --> 00:01:20.688
and production telemetry should be
reviewed together so teams can see whether

14
00:01:20.768 --> 00:01:23.873
quality is improving or drifting.

15
00:01:23.953 --> 00:01:28.557
Reliability problems can become safety
problems.

16
00:01:28.637 --> 00:01:35.275
A tool timeout may cause the agent to
answer without current information.

17
00:01:35.355 --> 00:01:38.566
A retry loop may duplicate actions.

18
00:01:38.646 --> 00:01:45.606
A cost spike may indicate runaway
retrieval or poorly bounded task planning.

19
00:01:45.686 --> 00:01:52.966
Low-confidence or unsupported claims may
lead users to act on weak information.

20
00:01:53.046 --> 00:02:00.541
Monitoring should help teams detect these
patterns before they become incidents.

21
00:02:00.621 --> 00:02:06.509
Quality monitoring should be tied to
ownership and improvement.

22
00:02:06.589 --> 00:02:13.013
Teams need to know who reviews evaluation
failures, who tunes prompts,

23
00:02:13.093 --> 00:02:15.663
who fixes tool reliability,

24
00:02:15.743 --> 00:02:21.310
and who decides when an agent is ready for
broader deployment.

25
00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:28.349
Security, reliability, and user experience
are connected in agent systems.

26
00:02:28.429 --> 00:02:33.140
Observability should help teams improve
all three.
